A||||21||Fiero5||Bad accident-Fieros were just barely not involved!||||11||
Z||000000||Fiero5||10-24-2001||01:50 PM||||We were coming home the other day, and we had just barely turned onto our road when we heard this squeeling noise. Then WHAM!!!<P>I could see an accident had happened which certainly fit the sounds, so I went and got the digital camcorder and quickly came back. Here is some of what I captured:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Accident1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident2.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident3.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident4.jpg"> <P>I really enjoyed the lady that was in the red car taking a moment to smoke a cig, next to her own accident!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident5.jpg"> <P>Steve||||reg||11
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||10-24-2001||01:52 PM||||Ouch!  Baretta=Totalled, new GM Truck $2000-$4000 in damage... how's that sound?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero5||10-24-2001||02:08 PM||||Here are a few more...<P>Just gotta have one more puff!!!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident7.jpg"> <P>Here it appeared that she was feeling pretty crappy now. She didn't have her seat belt on, and her drivers seat was still torn away from the floor! Now THAT is a rear end hit!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident6.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident8.jpg"> <P>The ambulance finally showed up<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident9.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident91.jpg"> <P>Apparently the lady in the red car was sitting facing south (to our left) waiting to turn onto our road. She was waiting for a friend we know in a black truck to turn right onto our road. While the two were waiting for each other to turn, the big black truck screamed up behind her. The young kid driving the "new" truck didn't see her until it was too late. Now she was stopped with her foot on the brake. He nailed her so hard, she swung around pushing even harder on her brake pedal from the shear force. She came skidding around from the south bound lane that she was in, to ending up facing north in the northbound lane. OUCH!<P>Here is what the new truck looked like<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident92.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident93.jpg"> ||||reg||9
Z||000003||Tigger||10-24-2001||02:16 PM||||Whoops!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>LOL, smok'in a cigarette next to the car after a nasty rear end crash.  Some people.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fiero5||10-24-2001||02:19 PM||||A few more<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident94.jpg"> <P>Hmmm, those rims look awefull familiar  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident95.jpg"> <P>This lady waving her hands is a friend of ours and was a witness. Her son was the one in the small black truck waiting to turn right. She works at the Post Office up the street and was walking home. She watched the whole thing in horror, which adding to the accident was the fact that she saw her son almost get hit by the red Beretta as it was thrown around right at him! He quickly stepped on the gas and pulled forward so her on coming car wouldn't hit him.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident96.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident97.jpg"> <P>Since both vehicles were in opposit lanes, and with the Police, wreckers and such, traffic was halted completely for over a half hour.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident98.jpg"> <P>Here are some shots of some of the skid marks<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident99.jpg"> <P>||||reg||11
Z||000005||Fiero5||10-24-2001||02:26 PM||||More skid marks<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident991.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident992.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident993.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident994.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident995.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident996.jpg"> <P>Well, she is really hurting now, as she is complaining that she is feeling really stiff and sore all over. Soooo...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident997.jpg"> <P>||||reg||11
Z||000006||Fiero5||10-24-2001||02:27 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident998.jpg"> <P>Last shot..<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/accident999.jpg"> <P>I wonder how she made out? That kid driving the new black truck that smacked her looked like he was only in his early 20's at best.<P><BR>Steve<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||beer_stud_21||10-24-2001||03:19 PM||||What is it I smell???  Is it a quad 4 conversion??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>-marlin||||reg||1
Z||000008||fierospeeder||10-24-2001||03:44 PM||||I do this, but i know a lot of other people who dont do it.  <P>It says it in our driving rule book also.<P>That when your going to make a left hand turn, keep your wheels straight, so just in case of a rear collision you wont get hit by uncoming traffic.<P>MAN, i got to get a digital camera.  I thought about hooking up a video camera to my car and recording everything i drive.  Should only cost few hundred bucks.||||reg||1
Z||000009||stsmithgt||10-24-2001||03:54 PM||||Where did the lady finally throw here cigarette butt?  In a pool of gas would have been exciting. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  It probably ended up on the ground like what most smokers do.  Some "lady" through one our her window on the freeway yesterday right in front of me.  Sparks were flying everywhere.  I thought it was going to land on my car since my sunroof was off.  It stunk too. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  More dang fires start that way.  Those things aren't called ASH trays for nothing.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||Jaei Sun||10-24-2001||04:23 PM||||The beretta that got hit is a z26 it's either a weak quad 4 ('94 last year of quad4 for the beretta I believe) or it's a automatic v6 with the 3100 (most likely).<p>[This message has been edited by Jaei Sun (edited 10-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||FieroRacer||10-24-2001||05:44 PM||||I say, more parts for our cars||||reg||1
Z||000012||Standard||10-24-2001||06:04 PM||||95 was actually the last year for the Quad 4.  Bad year, they added balance shafts, sucked a buncha hp from the engine.  In 96 they went to the 2.4l twin cam, which is pretty much the same thing, except with a smaller bore and longer stroke than the 2.3.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Fierowrecker||10-24-2001||09:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stsmithgt:<BR><B>Where did the lady finally throw here cigarette butt?  In a pool of gas would have been exciting.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  It probably ended up on the ground like what most smokers do.  Some "lady" through one our her window on the freeway yesterday right in front of me.  Sparks were flying everywhere.  I thought it was going to land on my car since my sunroof was off.  It stunk too.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  More dang fires start that way.  Those things aren't called ASH trays for nothing.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You left coasters are way too sensitive...<BR>Out here in the northwoods, we throw fusies into the state and federal forests to clear the underbrush so we can see what we are a hunting...<BR>Besides, with all that smog, how can you smell a tiny cigarette?<BR>And the ash is good for the soil, I dump all my woodstove ash onto my garden to increase the fertillity...<BR>BTW, if you LOOK at the pics, there isn't any leaking fluids on the ground...||||reg||1
Z||000014||Raydar||10-24-2001||10:41 PM||||Let me tell you...<BR>I used to smoke. For fifteen years. I've been quit since 88.<BR>However, if I still smoked and someone nailed me as hard as she got nailed, I'd be suckin' 'em down. One right after the other. Just works that way. If you've never smoked, you wouldn't understand. Glad I don't anymore.<P>Hope everybody gets okay. I'm amazed that nobody was hurt worse.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||9
