Z||000016||BlackStang95||10-25-2001||02:35 AM||||Damn, she sure got whacked hard.  Worst accident I ever saw was a Tempo take a sharp (15 mph) onramp way too fast and fall down a steep gully (no guard rail).  It wrapped sideways around a tree, killed 2 and messed up another.  ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Tigger||10-25-2001||09:09 AM||||I don't smoke so I guess I don't know, but if you really have to light up after something like that, don't smoke right next to your car.  Lighting up a cigarette at the scene of an accident is just Stoopid.||||reg||1
Z||000018||rogergarrison||10-25-2001||09:26 AM||||I have those same wheels on my Lumina van !! as long as no one was hurt, it was a good thing, broke up a boring day and got rid of another road hoging 4X4, at least for a while.||||reg||1
Z||000019||Black86SE||10-25-2001||06:14 PM||||There is nothing wrong with 4x4's. I one one now along with my Fiero. I wouldn't give it up for anything. I also owned a Bronco II once and it was 4 wheel drice also. I rolled that my senior year in high school. Just before all the busses came through. When they did come through, the kids got a good look at why they shouldn't screw around while it is wet and driving a stick.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000020||rogergarrison||10-25-2001||07:36 PM||||4X4's do have their place, if you live in the country, or somewhere like Idaho. I personally think that most places like Indiana and Ohio have no need for 4X4 trucks on the hiways except for some business purpose like construction crews. Ive never seen a situation where I needed a 4X4 to get around. I can get where I want in a regular car unless theres a 12" blizzard, and nothings open then anyway to go to. For off road, there fine. 4 wheel drive cars or all wheel drive is fine for hiway if you think you need it. At least those type vehicles (like Subaru) are fine because if they rear end you, at least there bumper doesnt come crashing thru your window, it hits the bumper like its supposed to. Not to mention the big knobby tires that throw rocks into your windshield on the hiways (twice).||||reg||1
Z||000021||stsmithgt||10-26-2001||04:28 PM||||A tiny cirarette "butt" can put out a hell of a lot of stench especially if the filter is smoldering for how small they are.  Besides, roadside fires tend to create accidents and big traffic jams if the smoke covers the roadway and it's a big waist of time for the fire dept. to have to come and put it out because someone didn't want that smelly thing in their ash tray. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">  I'm not too annoyed with it all.  I'm just putting in my 2 cents worth. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>My work of art.(in progress.)    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/carpicsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
